From: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: nss: tell the driver the AP_VLAN of a 4addr station

With NSS Wi-Fi offload, ieee80211_set_sta_4addr() passes the AP_VLAN of a
4addr (WDS) station to drv_sta_set_4addr(), so the driver can set up the
NSS ext vdev of that AP_VLAN. drv_sta_set_4addr() turned it back into the
AP with get_bss_sdata() first. ath11k then never configured the ext vdev
(no WDS peer, no 4addr allow, no ext vdev up), and the firmware kept
handing every frame of the station to the host as a 4addr exception,
which is dropped: a WDS station associates but passes no data.

Keep the AP_VLAN for drivers with NSS offload, as drv_set_key() already
does. With offload the AP_VLAN is added to the driver
(ieee80211_do_open() calls drv_add_interface() for it), so the
check_sdata_in_driver() that follows still holds.

Tested on a Xiaomi AX6000 (NSS FW 12.5-210) with a QCA9887 (ath10k) as
the 4addr client, on QCN9074 (5 GHz) and on the IPQ5018 radio (2.4 GHz):
the client's own traffic goes from no frames to ping and TCP both ways.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
@@ -1699,7 +1699,9 @@ static inline void drv_sta_set_4addr(str
 				     struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 				     struct ieee80211_sta *sta, bool enabled)
 {
-	sdata = get_bss_sdata(sdata);
+	if (!(sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN &&
+	      ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_NSS_OFFLOAD)))
+		sdata = get_bss_sdata(sdata);
 
 	might_sleep();
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(local->hw.wiphy);
